## Independent QA findings and disposition

1. Pre-existing flaky test `TestReviewerEnvironmentDoesNotReachChecksOrStages` (`internal/liverun/resolve_test.go`): fails
   ~22% under `make test` on BOTH base e1770da and this tree (QA measured 13/60 each). Cause: 1 s runner timeout vs.
   first-exec latency of a freshly written script on macOS. Out of this bead's declared scope; reported to the parent as a
   follow-on. Any red `make test` run attributable solely to this test was rerun.
2. `killGroup` lacked a `pid > 0` guard (kill(-0) would signal etude's own group; unreachable today). FOLDED: guard +
   `errInvalidPID` + `TestKillGroup_RejectsNonPositivePid`.
3. Success-path group kill was documented only in run.md. FOLDED: one clause in the replay/bench/retro `--timeout` rows and
   the gates.md check paragraph. Also added the CHANGELOG `[Unreleased] / Fixed` entry matching the A01/A15 precedent.
4. The `USER` seat-allowlist repair rides in this commit (disclosed in the plan; adjudicated by the plan gate).

## Known limitations (documented, not defects)

Not a sandbox: a child calling `setsid`/`setpgid` escapes (QA reproduced with `perl setpgrp`). Zombies may linger until
reaped. Non-Unix keeps direct-child cancellation only. The pgid-reuse window is bounded to the synchronous post-Wait kill.

